A||||12||Formula 18||Windsheild... DIY? ||||5||
Z||000000||Formula 18||06-15-2000||07:37 AM||||My winshield cracked the other day (damn counrty dirt roads) and I was wondering a few things? Is this a job that you can do your-self, well I guess ALL job CAN be done your-self, but I'm I better off to get it done by the pro's??? What does a used glass go for? I've seen 5 Fieros in local bone-yards and thought I could just get a glass from that. If this turns out to be a PITA I'll probally just get it done but if it is only a weekend father son thing I'll keep you guys updated. ANY i mean ANY help is greatly appreacated. <P>Brian ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Will||06-15-2000||08:51 AM||||The windshield is bonded in, which makes it harder to replace than a gasket and lockstrip piece, but not impossible. I haven't done it myself, but my father says it's doable.<BR>I'll have to be replacing mine sometime before it come up for inspection again in OCT.||||reg||1
Z||000002||wkayl||06-15-2000||09:23 AM||||$165.00 here in Loveland CO||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula||06-15-2000||11:51 AM||||my new winsheild installed was $98, but I didn't get a warranty because the guy said there was some rust on the edge...???? (plastic rust I guess) ||||reg||1
Z||000004||ROB MAC||06-15-2000||11:55 AM||||Doesn't your insurance cover that? You just pay the deductable and lots of glass companies will pay that for you just to get the job. I do most doable jobs on my car but that was one I was glad I didn't. It's a two man job and if you aren't quick you can get a bad seal. If you are still going to do ittalk to the pro's and learn all the tricks.||||reg||1
Z||000005||prof bobo||06-15-2000||12:58 PM||||Say Formula, the windshield is mounted to the frame, not the body.  If you got rust there, you got deep troubles brewing . . .||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula 18||06-15-2000||06:45 PM||||Thanks for the help guys... I was wondering if I could do it with my dad or if it was something that was a major undertaking. Can some one tell me about how it is mounted to the body? and what's the deal with the rust? If it is more than my $250 deductable and/or a pain in the ass i'll just get it done&gt; <P>Anyone actually done it??? If so how?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula||06-15-2000||08:52 PM||||It actually looked more like dirt than rust, but I decided not to get the warranty anyway.  They wanted a lot more for it.||||reg||1
Z||000008||84 Indy||06-15-2000||09:33 PM||||The windsheild in a fiero is installed with a special urethane adhesive and is actually a structual part of the car. I got this info from the factory service manual for my 86 .<BR>Let the pros do it. They use a heated urethane to install it.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Phaeton||06-16-2000||12:23 AM||||Two thirds of my windshield came loose on a really big bump.  After comparing where it came loose with the spots it stayed put, that urethane adhesive is VERY important to put on correctly!<P>The urethane did not bond to the glass on my Fiero, no problem with the frame side.  No history on who did the windshield install, but the glass should have broken up as it came loose, not just popped off whole.<P>So my two pennies is Let the Pro do it.||||reg||12
Z||000010||olympic||06-16-2000||02:30 AM||||  Shop around.  Prices can vary alot!!  Some places will do it for dirt cheap if you pay cash without a receipt.  <BR>    Glass is insanely expensive here in Saskatchewan.  One place wanted $600 for a winshield in one of my taxis.  I went to another place and they replaced it for $120 cash.  Later on, a friend told me that the shop just tells the glass manufacturer that the windshield was damaged in shipping so they get a refund and sell it to you for next to nothing.||||reg||1
Z||000011||fierodave||06-16-2000||06:03 AM||||Triunph auto glass.......nationwide installer  $135.00 tax & molding included.. Triumph will meet or beat any competitors prices.<BR>Triumph a division of Diamond Glass Co.<BR>(Damnn sounded like a commercial)<P>lol  but I have had over a dozen windshields done for Fiero's local and there a good Co. to deal with<BR>FD||||reg||1
Z||000012||Formula 18||06-16-2000||11:18 AM||||Ok.. So we'll let the Pros put it in. Next Question. Can I go to the Junkie and get a new Glass?? There are about 5 around here. Is it had to pull off w/o breaking it?? <P>Any tips on this. ||||reg||1
